it's a move that's rekindling the debate  over the future of spain's catalonia  region and its independence movement  the results of the voting session of  monday the 8th of march  the european parliament has removed the  immunity of khalis pujdemont  former catalan president and two  associates all of whom have seats in the  assembly  they fled abroad in 2017 following an  independence referendum  and subsequent declaration of  independence which the spanish  government deemed illegal  it is a sad day for european parliament  we have lost our immunity  but the european parliament has lost  more than that  and as a result european democracy too  this is a clear case of political  persecution  the decision could help madrid's bid to  extradite the trio  carla's pujdamon tony comey and carla  poncetti have been charged with sedition  in spain  quiddimont and comey are also accused of  misusing public funds  but poncetti who's based in scotland  told al jazeera they're confident of  winning an appeal  we will contest this lifting of immunity  in the european court of justice because  our claim is that this is a political  prosecution and as such  our immunity should not have been lifted  that will take some time but we have  very strong arguments and very strong  hopes  that we will prevail on this appeal  the 2017 independence referendum stoked  major tensions between the spanish  government  and the leaders of catalonia an  autonomous region of seven and a half  million people  the bitterness of the debate has  diminished since socialist prime  minister pedro sanchez came to power in  madrid in 2018.  but in last month's regional elections  separatist parties gained four  additional seats in the catalan  parliament  the independent is parties who come from  the  right to the center to the left so there  are all kinds of  uh political opinions in the independent  these parties  they want this majority in the catalan  parliament so this proves that we still  have the  the elephant in the room meanwhile a  belgian court recently rejected spain's  request to extradite another former  catalan cabinet member  and it's far from clear how authorities  here and in scotland  will cooperate with madrid now nadine  barber al jazeera
 

